course: dictionary
lesson: 12942
title: Excavator: a digging machine or a careful digger
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Use the clues in the sentence to pick the right one. «The excavator scooped up mud and rocks from the building site.» The clues are scooped, mud and building site, so an excavator here is a big digging machine.
explain: The same word can also mean a person. «The excavator carefully brushed the dust from the old clay pot.» Brushing dust off a pot slowly and carefully points to a person who digs to find old objects. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Excavate is the verb, meaning to dig out carefully. «The workers will excavate the trench before the pipes go in.» Excavator is the noun for the machine or the person who does the digging.
fact: An excavator is a big machine with an arm and a bucket for digging up earth and rocks.
fact: An excavator can also be a person who digs carefully at a site to find old objects.
fact: «Excavate» means to dig out earth carefully, especially to find things buried long ago.
fact: A mini excavator is a small version of the big machine, often used for garden and road work.
fact: Stay well back from a working excavator. Its heavy arm can move suddenly.
exercise: «The excavator lifted the heavy rocks into the lorry.» What is an excavator in this sentence? | A kind of bird | A person who studies old pots | A small house on wheels | *A big digging machine
exercise: «The excavator carefully brushed dust from the bones.» What is an excavator in this sentence? | A digging machine with a bucket | *A person who digs carefully to find old objects | A builder who paints walls | A spade for the garden
exercise: «The team will excavate the old well next week.» Find and copy the verb. | week | next | *excavate | team
test: «The mini excavator dug a small trench beside the path.» What is a mini excavator? | *A small digging machine | A tiny spade used by children | A boat for the river | A type of tree
test: Why must you stay well back from a working excavator? | *Its heavy arm can move suddenly and hurt you | It is only a toy and cannot hurt anyone | It is painted in bright colours | It is trying to hide from you
exam: Which sentence uses excavator to mean a person? | *The excavator carefully uncovered a clay pot from the old field. | The excavator roared and turned left. | The excavator was parked by the gate. | The excavator's bucket was full of gravel.
